WEBVTT

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:24.400
You know, this one time,...

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.560
...we were kind of playing
around and I hugged Hatsumi.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.900
Her body was so warm,...

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.400
...and my heart was pounding
so hard just from touching her.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:43.130
I couldn't believe that I
was holding her in my arms.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.600
I was so happy but I wondered
how long this happiness would last.

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:58.260
And it made me so
sad that I wanted to cry.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.060
I want to see you but I can't
see you because it hurts so much.

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:11.130
I'm sure I must
be missing something...

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:14.300
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.430
(Yami, the Hat and the Book traveler)
...and that's why my
prayer hasn't been answered.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:25.430
I had always believed
that what I saw before me...

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:32.230
...was the only truth there was.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:40.060
But now I know
there isn't just one world.

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:49.530
There are a thousand worlds called
"if" and I don't know which way to turn.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:55.360
I want to see you but
I can't see you; where are you now?

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:58.560
I'll find you no matter the cost.

00:01:58.760 --> 00:02:06.330
I've wandered into the
labyrinth of your eyes.

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:10.300
Even if the darkness bars my path...

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:16.300
...even if my weak heart
is led astray, I won't give up.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:21.300
I'll keep searching for you.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.100
Hazuki.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.200
Hatsumi!

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.600
Try a sexier pose!

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:56.930
No, look at me, don't be shy!

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:02.430
Lean forward, that's good!

00:03:08.900 --> 00:03:11.400
After 5 straight days of
rain, it finally stopped.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:18.760
But my heart is not broken yet.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:28.630
One week ago.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:18.300
Ever since that day, I
couldn't look at her face.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.100
The day before...

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.360
Hatsumi, are you feeling sick?

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:39.360
It's your birthday tomorrow.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.930
That's right, you'll be sixteen.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:51.400
Oh, we're having a party tomorrow,
come straight home, okay?

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.360
Have a good sleep tonight.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:11.260
Why that good bye sign?
Did she mix it up with good night?

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:19.330
12 hours ago

00:05:35.060 --> 00:05:36.500
Sister, sister...

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:44.330
Hatsumi never talks, but it's
like she whispers gently to me.

00:05:45.660 --> 00:05:48.960
It's like she's
saying, "Hazuki, it's okay."

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:57.230
I can always hear
her deep within my heart.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.160
To Ms. Hatsumi Higashi (envelope)
One hour ago

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:07.360
I can't stop thinking about
Hatsumi so much. It's not fair!

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:20.300
I, I... I am sorry.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:28.630
I'll go get some
bandages and medicine.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:35.700
One week ago

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.400
Azuma senpai, um...

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:44.260
It's for you, please accept it!

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:09.230
If I open this door, it'll be a mess.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:13.130
Somehow, I knew that.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:01.600
I am sorry, Hatsumi.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.400
Hazuki...

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.060
Hatsumi, you can talk!?

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:48.560
Hatsumi!

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:55.900
Hatsumi!

00:09:16.600 --> 00:09:17.400
Hatsumi...

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:23.730
I was feeling...

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:26.960
Hatsumi!

00:09:27.360 --> 00:09:27.930
Hatsumi!

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:35.660
Hatsumi was gone,
nowhere to be found.

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:40.730
To Ms. Hatsumi Higashi

00:09:50.560 --> 00:09:51.730
Sister...

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:57.860
Oh, I didn't make it in time!

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:02.100
Lilith will scold me.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.160
It's past midnight.

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.000
That lady is already sixteen now.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:18.600
Where did you take Hatsumi to?

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:23.400
I am looking for her. Now that
she's gone to another world,...

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.560
...I have to find her.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:27.800
So let me go!

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.200
Then, take me with you.

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:30.330
No way!

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:33.200
You're choking me!

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:35.100
Take me.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:41.230
Okay, but stop with the violence!

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:53.260
Well, you received the
souma of Eve, so you can travel.

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:54.700
Souma of Eve?

00:10:57.600 --> 00:10:58.760
Was that...?

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.260
Yep.

00:11:00.530 --> 00:11:04.760
It seems that letter opener
sucked up a lot of souma.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:18.600
Well then, shall we?

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:24.660
This way!

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:39.400
Limit height : 3.5 meters

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:56.700
It's about time to
travel to the next book.

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:03.530
Sometimes this life
doesn't go as you had hoped.

00:12:05.100 --> 00:12:07.960
The question is what do you do?

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:13.000
How about a story like this?

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:27.500
Watch out!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:28.630
You're in my way!

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:32.100
Huh, show off!

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:38.430
Here you go!

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:12.060
Night Train departing soon.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:14.830
All aboard!

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:19.930
You're late, Hazuki.
You almost missed the train.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.400
Have a nice trip.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:31.930
Night train departing, all board!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:37.930
The target is an
Asian man, alias Adam.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:45.330
His task is to bring back the
code to decipher the signal book.

00:13:45.560 --> 00:13:48.930
Of course, our opponent
is also after that code.

00:13:49.600 --> 00:13:55.300
And your first
mission is to assist Adam.

00:13:55.530 --> 00:13:56.330
Yes, sir.

00:13:56.860 --> 00:14:00.600
Listen, your task is just to back up.

00:14:01.060 --> 00:14:02.960
No need to go beyond that.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:09.560
During field training, you sent 3
of your coworkers to the hospital...

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:13.100
That's why they call
you the "final weapon."

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:19.730
Honestly, I am against this order
but this came from our chief...

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.630
...who happens to be your father...

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:25.530
I am counting on you.

00:14:38.760 --> 00:14:41.160
I'm confident I can do it.

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:57.530
When is the next stop?

00:14:57.530 --> 00:14:59.460
This is a non-stop train.

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:00.900
What is the arrival time?

00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:02.930
7:00 AM.

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:05.130
So that's 8 hours..

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:10.630
I see your staff are also
on board, is everything okay?

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:14.800
There was an anonymous call
that there is a bomb on this train.

00:15:16.630 --> 00:15:20.860
Our enemy is trying to detonate
the explosives in the cargo car.

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:23.900
We suspect their spy is on this train.

00:15:25.960 --> 00:15:30.130
We're here to prevent
such an act, will you help us?

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:31.630
Yes, sir!

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.560
Also, keep it to yourself!

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:55.060
No need for this.

00:16:05.300 --> 00:16:08.560
Is someone in there?

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:35.230
Landed!

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:39.260
Ouch!! That's awful!!

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:43.500
Why does this Lilith have to be here?

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:45.830
Answer me, bad cholesterol!

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:48.000
Nobody calls me bad cholesterol!?

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:50.330
I've got a nice name, it's Ken!

00:16:50.330 --> 00:16:52.330
I am not asking any such thing.

00:16:53.000 --> 00:16:57.760
I told you already, soldiers are
running around here with guns,

00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:03.700
If somebody in a spooky outfit
like yours goes out there,...

00:17:04.360 --> 00:17:06.900
...they'll burn you for sure!

00:17:06.900 --> 00:17:08.230
It's not a big deal!

00:17:08.630 --> 00:17:13.460
I don't want anymore trouble!

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:14.960
What about Hazuki?

00:17:14.960 --> 00:17:19.730
So, she is helping you look for Eve.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:23.130
How far is she going?

00:17:45.900 --> 00:17:47.060
Excuse me.

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.700
Who me?

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:03.230
Are you a sales man?

00:18:04.160 --> 00:18:06.330
Something like that.

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:10.400
Something like that? Check him.

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:26.830
It looks fine, sir.

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.330
Not done yet.

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:39.530
What have you done with it?!

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:41.900
Where did you hide it?

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:42.930
Hide what?

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:46.930
Don't fool me,
I have good sense of smell.

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:51.230
I can tell, something
about you is very fishy.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:54.600
I don't know what you want me to say.

00:18:56.230 --> 00:18:57.500
What's going on?

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:02.700
Is there a problem
with my secretary?

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:05.100
Your secretary?

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:12.130
I have important friends in your
home country, my name is Mr. Saiga.

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:28.600
Why did you come to help me?

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:37.900
I don't like those kind of people.

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:41.200
That's why you saved me?

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:45.760
It's only natural to help your mate,...

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:49.830
...especially someone
in the same profession.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:55.100
You must be Tiger of Siberia...

00:19:56.400 --> 00:19:59.200
It's been a while since
I was called by that name.

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:02.700
You're a legend in my organization.

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:06.660
Well, don't do anything crazy.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:25.230
I'll check on those two people.

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:28.460
Go ask the conductor about them.

00:20:36.160 --> 00:20:37.760
Where are you, Hada?

00:20:40.700 --> 00:20:41.360
Yes?

00:20:41.600 --> 00:20:43.660
I have something to ask you.

00:20:51.400 --> 00:20:52.300
Who are you?

00:20:53.460 --> 00:20:56.360
I'm in search of our enemy's spy.

00:20:57.730 --> 00:21:00.200
You seem to know something.

00:21:00.600 --> 00:21:01.630
I know nothing.

00:21:01.630 --> 00:21:02.600
What's your occupation?

00:21:02.900 --> 00:21:04.060
I am a diplomat.

00:21:04.060 --> 00:21:05.660
Here's my I.D.

00:21:10.730 --> 00:21:14.130
I have a sensitive sense of smell.

00:21:23.660 --> 00:21:27.860
It's unusual for a
diplomat to disguise as a man.

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:53.360
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:21:53.630 --> 00:21:59.800
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:02.630 --> 00:22:07.260
I will go there, praying.

00:22:07.830 --> 00:22:14.100
No matter the distance
between us, I will catch you.

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:21.930
That's a promise between you and I.

00:22:22.130 --> 00:22:29.230
Crying, cradling my memories,...

00:22:29.230 --> 00:22:35.760
..won't help even one
of my feelings to reach you.

00:22:37.360 --> 00:22:44.800
I will offer up an eternal prayer.

00:22:45.000 --> 00:22:51.430
I will never give up on what matters.

00:22:53.400 --> 00:23:00.330
I will find the dawn
between you and I,...

00:23:01.130 --> 00:23:08.760
...and meet the approaching daybreak.

00:23:09.260 --> 00:23:14.000
I will go there, praying.

00:23:14.860 --> 00:23:19.330
Oh, what will happen
to Youko? Punt punt...

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:21.630
Let's take a little peek.

00:23:50.030 --> 00:23:52.630
Next Time: Youko
Yami, the hat, and the Book Traveler.

00:23:53.200 --> 00:23:55.900
Stay tuned for the next episode.
